      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria (PHN) is an acquired chronic hemolytic anemia associated with an unusual susceptibility to hemolytic crisis, infection, and venous thrombosis which would be aggravated by a number of factors including surgery. We report a case of PHN undergoing percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty and discuss the corresponding perioperative management."},
